From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Fit the Phone keypad on the cover

The 748x720 cover counts as landscape, so Phone used its landscape keypad: the
number, the keys and the call buttons side by side, sized for a wide phone
screen. On the 352 dp cover the keys got 43% of the width, their letters broke
into ragged columns, and the call button column was too narrow, so the call,
delete and video call buttons ran off the right edge. Turned to 720x748, the
portrait keypad was worse: its rows overlapped.

In a small landscape window, which on this ROM means the whole cover:
- values-small-land gives the keys the full width and sizes delete and call
  for one row;
- OnigiriCoverDialpad puts the number, delete and call in the top row, next to
  the app bar, which shrinks to its overflow button while the keypad tab shows;
  video call goes away;
- DialtactsActivity moves create contact and search into the overflow menu on
  that tab, and keeps Phone in landscape, either way up, while it is on the
  cover, the way Samsung keeps it in portrait on the small covers of older
  Folds.
diff --git a/res/values-small-land/dimens.xml b/res/values-small-land/dimens.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8b4ef08
--- /dev/null
+++ b/res/values-small-land/dimens.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<resources>
+    <!-- Onigiri: delete and call buttons that fit in the top row in a small landscape window,
+         and keys with less inset than values-land gives them. -->
+    <dimen name="dialpad_button_icon_size">24.0dp</dimen>
+    <dimen name="dialpad_dial_button_height_usa">44.0dp</dimen>
+    <dimen name="dialpad_dial_button_width_land">56.0dp</dimen>
+    <dimen name="dialpad_dual_sim_call_button_height">56.0dp</dimen>
+    <dimen name="dialpad_keypad_endmargin">8.0dp</dimen>
+    <dimen name="dialpad_keypad_startmargin">8.0dp</dimen>
+</resources>
diff --git a/res/values-small-land/integers.xml b/res/values-small-land/integers.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..adaa922
--- /dev/null
+++ b/res/values-small-land/integers.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<resources>
+    <!-- Onigiri: a small landscape window, such as the whole Flip5 cover. The keys take the full
+         width (values-land gives them 43%); OnigiriCoverDialpad puts the number, delete and call
+         in the top row. -->
+    <integer name="dialpad_keypad_weight">1000</integer>
+    <integer name="dialpad_view_width_weight_phone">1000</integer>
+</resources>
